# class: governance-files
# schema: file | purpose | sections | role-co-ownership | source
# source-glob: README.md + CONTRIBUTING.md + SECURITY.md + CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md + CHANGELOG.md
# recipe: novel
# authored: 2026-05-23
# Recipe: per file extract purpose, one-line summary of each top-level section, ginee/role co-ownership cross-refs (per D25 bindings.md).

README.md | Primary repo landing page and evaluator quickstart | Sections: quickstart-60s-demo (gh release download + pwsh install.ps1 -Demo); features bullet list (tool-agnostic / real-time / 4-views-3-layouts / themes / fetcher / internal-only); how-it-works summary; docs site link; license badge; "AI-implemented end-to-end via ginee" note | team-lead (primary); solution-architect (feature accuracy review) | @README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md | Contributor guide — how to file issues, propose changes, run locally, edit docs | Sections: how-this-project-is-built (ginee multi-agent); filing-an-issue (bug-report / feature-request templates; ginee:ready auto-label; team-lead pickup); proposing-a-change (issue-first; full Phase 1-8 lifecycle; wire-contract/NFR changes need CR/ADR); local-dev (start.ps1 pointer); doc-edits (routing table: architecture/ADRs/CRs/UI-options -> SA; mockup -> frontend-engineer; routing rules -> bindings.md); stack-pointers table (8 key doc paths) | team-lead (primary); solution-architect (doc-edit routing accuracy) | @CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md | Security policy | Sections: supported-versions (main HEAD = yes; pre-1.0 tagged = no; no LTS); reporting-a-vulnerability (GitHub Security Advisories; no public issues for suspected vulns; 7-day acknowledgement target); scope (NFR-04 internal-only; Write group X-Api-Key; Read API unauthenticated by design); not-a-security-issue (feature requests / doc typos / functional bugs without CIA impact / NFR-04-matching behaviour) | solution-architect (scope accuracy per NFR-04 / SAD §8); team-lead (governance) | @SECURITY.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md | Code of conduct | Sections: scope (all project spaces: issues / PRs / discussions / hosted docs); reporting (confidential via GitHub Security Advisories); enforcement (Contributor Covenant v2.1 guidance) | team-lead | @CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CHANGELOG.md | Changelog — Keep a Changelog format + SemVer | Sections: Unreleased (no tagged releases yet; see commit history); format-note (based on keepachangelog.com v1.1.0 + SemVer; pre-1.0 breaking changes between minor versions) | team-lead | @CHANGELOG.md
